    description: "Yesoul is better known for exercise bikes, and this walking pad with long handrails is its senior model. The listing leads with safety: a one-tap emergency button for instant stopping, extended handrails for support, and a safety key that cuts power. The belt has six layers with six shock absorbers, the motor holds a steady speed between 0.6 and 3.8 mph, and the capacity is 300 lb. An LED display shows time, calories, steps, speed and distance, a remote adjusts speed and mode, and there are holders for a phone and a cup. Amazon lists the weight at 48 lb, light for a machine with rails, and the warranty is one year. It was about $240 on Amazon on 9 November 2026, the lowest price on this page. Two things to weigh up. The 0.6 mph start is not as gentle as the Redliro machines' 0.3 mph, though still slow. And the remote is convenient but can be dropped; make sure the user knows where the stop button is and always clips on the key.",
  },
  {
    id: "lastforever-seniors",
    name: "Lastforever Walking Treadmill",
    brand: "Lastforever",
    category: "Senior treadmill with full-length rails and rail controls",
    badge: "No-Bend Controls",
