            short front bar helps only while you face forward; and a pad with no rail at all suits
            only confident, steady walkers. After that, look for a slow start speed and a weight
            rating with plenty of margin. Our guide to <a href="/best-treadmills-for-seniors/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">treadmills for seniors</a> covers full-size machines with consoles and cushioned decks if you have more space.
          </p>
